A little girl, Léa — toddler proportions about four heads tall, soft rounded features, rounded belly, brown eyes, loose chin-length dark brown straight hair with bangs at eyebrows, wearing an orange long-sleeve swim shirt and an orange scaled mermaid tail ending in a wide flowing fin, with a narrow green seaweed bracelet knotted around her left wrist — swims forward in the foreground along a pale sand channel of the coral reef, holding out both hands curled around a long green seaweed strand that has a single tight knot tied in its middle with trailing loose ends. In the midground behind her, Marc — an adult man with mature build, brown eyes, short combed dark brown wavy hair with a side part, short stubble beard, wearing a green long-sleeve swim shirt and a green scaled merman tail ending in a crescent fin with a black waistband — swims alongside Henri, an elderly man with stooped posture, brown eyes, white wavy short hair, full white beard, white mustache, wearing a white long-sleeve swim shirt, red scarf, and a grey scaled merman tail ending in a broad fin, both watching Léa with calm attentiveness. Nearby, Jules — a young school-age boy with rounded features, blue eyes, short combed dark brown straight hair with bangs, wearing a blue short-sleeve swim shirt, a brown kelp-cord belt, and a blue scaled merman tail ending in a pointed fin — swims beside them with his eyes fixed on the knotted seaweed strand. Sunlit deep blue-green water fills the wide view of the undersea coral reef, where cream and pale rose branching coral heads and sea fans line the banks of the winding sand path under the autumn sea.

