An elderly man, Henri — elderly proportions with stooped posture, brown eyes, short combed white wavy hair, full white beard, white mustache, small mole under left eye and on right cheek, wearing a white long-sleeve swim shirt with rolled sleeves, a red knitted sailor's scarf, and a grey scaled merman tail ending in a heavy broad fin — turns his body at the mouth of the coral arch in the midground, raising one arm to wave outward toward the shadowed tunnel entrance while looking straight ahead along the opening. The pale cream and rose-beige coral arch spans across the reef wall, rising twice the height of the merfolk, its dark opening leading through the rock. Smooth ochre sand and rounded coral heads cover the foreground floor in the clear sunlit water of the autumn reef in this wide view.

