In a close-up at the mouth of the coral arch, Léa — a toddler little girl with soft rounded features, brown eyes, loose chin-length dark brown straight hair with eyebrow bangs, wearing an orange long-sleeve swim shirt, an orange scaled mermaid tail, and a narrow green seaweed bracelet knotted around her left wrist — is framed from the waist up beside a thick pale cream coral pillar on the left, her hands cupped beside her open mouth as her focused gaze looks out across the distant open water beyond the archway. Overhead, the rounded coral rim curves across the upper frame, opening out into the sunlit blue-green water of the shoal where the distant silhouette of a head rises above a rock.

